    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Project KO11 Is Proof That Geely Wants To \"Knock Out\" Range Rover, Launches Next Year in Europe\nBYD Is Spicing Up Its UK Offering With Truckman Official Accessories for the Shark Pickup Truck\n16 photos\nPhoto: BYD\nBYD bet that cool accessories could boost sales of its Shark pickup trucks in the UK, so it partnered with Truckman to offer approved accessories to its customers. The British accessories specialist will supply a wide range of load bed hardtops, tonneau covers and cross bars. Customers will be able to order them directly from BYD retailers in the UK.\nWhile Europeans are not huge pickup truck fans, they occasionally buy them, either for work or leisure. Surprisingly, most of them are midsize trucks, with the most popular being the Ford Ranger and Toyota Hilux. Compact pickups have not caught traction, with Renault/Dacia selling a truck based on the Duster crossover in very limited quantities.\nUnsurprisingly, BYD is also entering the European market with a midsize truck called Shark. The Chinese carmaker just started sales in the UK in September, with plans to expand to EU countries in 2027. And since a pickup truck is not merely a vehicle, but a platform, BYD correctly anticipated that a successful market launch requires a compelling accessory offer.\nIn the UK, BYD partnered with Truckman to design and build the official accessories for the Shark. The British company has over 40 years of experience in supplying accessories for pickups, so it was a natural choice for BYD. Since British pickup truck owners are just as fond of pimping up their vehicles as those across the Pond, Truckman should significantly boost BYD Shark's capabilities and appeal.\nHardtops are among the most popular truck accessories, and the new partnership doesn't disappoint. The Grand Hardtop option is color-coded to match the vehicle. It comes with pop-out windows, rear window heating, and remote central locking. This provides a weatherproof cover for the truck's bed without compromising on looks.\nPhoto: BYD The M-Series hardtop provides a more rugged alternative, which sports a powder-coated finish. Gull-wing side windows make it easy to load and unload from both the sides and the rear of the truck. This is also more versatile than the Grand Hardtop, providing multiple mounting options for a wide range of accessories.\nTwo Truckman tonneau covers will be offered, one with a manually retractable cover and the other electrically actuated. The latter can be remotely opened and closed via a smartphone app. Both covers feature an IP56 weather resistance rating and a T-slot system to fit optional cargo bars. These include the Heavy Duty Black Cross Bars, which can withstand a dynamic load of 200kg and a static load of 360kg.\nA cool accessory for those who want easy access to tools, camping equipment, and appliances in the bed is the DragMat. This slides in and out of the bed and can handle over 100 kg (220 lb) of cargo. It can also provide extra protection against scuffs and scratches for the load bed, if that's something a truck owner should worry about.\nThe BYD Shark is an off-road-capable plug-in hybrid that gives its more seasoned rivals a run for their money. It uses a 1.5-litre turbocharged four-cylinder petrol engine and a pair of electric motors, one at the front and the other at the rear. These are powered by a 32.2 kWh battery, one of the largest in the segment. Total power reaches 430 hp, developed by the two electric motors, with the petrol engine acting as a generator.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nBYD Shark BYD truckman truck accessories\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Cristian Agatie\nAfter his childhood dream of becoming a \"tractor operator\" didn't pan out, Cristian turned to journalism, first in print and later moving to online media. His top interests are electric vehicles and new energy solutions. Full profile\nUP NEXT This Shelby GT350 Just Sold for Hilariously Cheap – But There’s a Catch",
